1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:05,048
Multiply a plus b by itself five
times, and you fill a whole page with

2
00:00:05,048 --> 00:00:05,948
working.

3
00:00:06,166 --> 00:00:09,849
But a triangle of numbers
writes the answer in seconds.

4
00:00:09,849 --> 00:00:12,571
One, five, ten, ten, five, one.

5
00:00:13,021 --> 00:00:16,930
Diya found this triangle in a
library book during a free period.

6
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:21,529
How can a simple triangle know the
answer to a long multiplication?

7
00:00:22,029 --> 00:00:23,692
It is called Pascal's triangle.

8
00:00:23,692 --> 00:00:25,957
Let us build it, and see why it works.

9
00:00:26,607 --> 00:00:28,372
First, some small powers.

10
00:00:28,372 --> 00:00:29,647
Watch the pattern.

11
00:00:29,997 --> 00:00:32,435
a plus b to the power zero is one.

12
00:00:32,435 --> 00:00:35,224
To the power one, it is just a plus b.

13
00:00:35,624 --> 00:00:36,732
Now square it.

14
00:00:36,732 --> 00:00:39,213
Picture a square with side a plus b.

15
00:00:39,213 --> 00:00:44,302
It splits into an a by a square, two
a by b strips, and a b by b square.

16
00:00:45,052 --> 00:00:49,545
So a plus b squared is a squared,
plus two a b, plus b squared.

17
00:00:49,545 --> 00:00:52,421
The numbers in front are one, two, one.

18
00:00:53,171 --> 00:00:57,160
Cube it, and the numbers in
front are one, three, three, one.

19
00:00:57,810 --> 00:00:59,468
Now build the triangle.

20
00:00:59,468 --> 00:01:02,966
Write a one at the top,
and ones down both edges.

21
00:01:03,366 --> 00:01:07,274
Every number inside is the sum
of the two numbers just above it.

22
00:01:07,674 --> 00:01:09,281
One plus one is two.

23
00:01:09,281 --> 00:01:12,868
One plus two is three,
and two plus one is three.

24
00:01:13,268 --> 00:01:14,168
Keep going.

25
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:16,066
One, four, six, four, one.

26
00:01:16,066 --> 00:01:18,687
Then one, five, ten, ten, five, one.

27
00:01:19,287 --> 00:01:23,456
Each row gives the numbers in front
for the next power of a plus b.

28
00:01:24,106 --> 00:01:25,216
Side by side.

29
00:01:25,216 --> 00:01:29,989
Multiplying out a plus b to the fourth
takes many steps, and many chances

30
00:01:29,989 --> 00:01:30,889
to slip.

31
00:01:31,181 --> 00:01:35,175
The triangle gives one, four,
six, four, one in one line.

32
00:01:35,175 --> 00:01:37,354
Then we only fill in the powers.

33
00:01:37,954 --> 00:01:38,885
Now you try.

34
00:01:38,885 --> 00:01:42,254
How many terms are there in
a plus b to the power six?

35
00:01:42,254 --> 00:01:43,365
Six, or seven?

36
00:01:43,365 --> 00:01:44,521
Pause and decide.

37
00:01:47,721 --> 00:01:48,621
Seven!

38
00:01:48,226 --> 00:01:51,215
The number of terms is always
one more than the power.

39
00:01:51,865 --> 00:01:53,574
But why does adding work?

40
00:01:53,574 --> 00:01:54,505
Let us see.

41
00:01:54,855 --> 00:01:57,550
a plus b cubed is three
brackets multiplied together.

42
00:01:57,550 --> 00:01:59,853
From each bracket, we pick either a or b.

43
00:02:00,603 --> 00:02:04,386
To get a b squared, we pick b
from two of the three brackets.

44
00:02:04,386 --> 00:02:06,741
That can be done in three C two ways.

45
00:02:06,741 --> 00:02:07,641
Three.

46
00:02:08,035 --> 00:02:11,956
So the number in front of
a b squared is three C two.

47
00:02:11,956 --> 00:02:17,379
In general, row n holds n C zero,
n C one, and so on, up to n C n.

48
00:02:18,129 --> 00:02:22,259
A term in the next row can come from
a bracket giving a, or giving b.

49
00:02:22,259 --> 00:02:25,538
That is why each number is
the sum of the two above it.

50
00:02:26,288 --> 00:02:27,566
Look at row five.

51
00:02:27,566 --> 00:02:30,102
One, five, ten, ten, five, one.

52
00:02:30,102 --> 00:02:33,783
The same counts we got for
picking teams from five friends.

53
00:02:34,433 --> 00:02:37,451
Watch the expansion grow,
one power at a time.

54
00:02:37,851 --> 00:02:39,547
Power two, three terms.

55
00:02:39,547 --> 00:02:41,292
Power three, four terms.

56
00:02:41,292 --> 00:02:42,987
Power four, five terms.

57
00:02:42,987 --> 00:02:44,635
Power five, six terms.

58
00:02:45,035 --> 00:02:49,659
In every term, the power of a goes
down by one, and the power of b goes

59
00:02:49,659 --> 00:02:50,559
up by one.

60
00:02:50,551 --> 00:02:52,883
The two powers always add up to n.

61
00:02:53,483 --> 00:02:54,383
Quick one.

62
00:02:54,257 --> 00:02:57,317
Add up row four: one,
four, six, four, one.

63
00:02:57,317 --> 00:02:58,465
What do you get?

64
00:02:58,465 --> 00:02:59,559
Pause and think.

65
00:03:02,759 --> 00:03:03,659
Sixteen!

66
00:03:03,388 --> 00:03:05,308
That is two to the power four.

67
00:03:05,308 --> 00:03:09,581
Put a and b both equal to one, and a
plus b to the fourth becomes two to

68
00:03:09,581 --> 00:03:10,481
the fourth.

69
00:03:11,045 --> 00:03:12,026
Remember this.

70
00:03:12,026 --> 00:03:14,776
Each number is the sum
of the two above it.

71
00:03:14,776 --> 00:03:18,625
Row n gives the numbers in front
for a plus b to the power n.

72
00:03:19,325 --> 00:03:21,014
Now, one worked example.

73
00:03:21,364 --> 00:03:24,033
Expand x plus two, to the power four.

74
00:03:24,533 --> 00:03:25,433
Step one.

75
00:03:25,287 --> 00:03:28,975
Row four of the triangle is
one, four, six, four, one.

76
00:03:29,725 --> 00:03:30,625
Step two.

77
00:03:30,510 --> 00:03:33,335
The powers of x go down from four to zero.

78
00:03:33,335 --> 00:03:36,160
The powers of two go up from zero to four.

79
00:03:36,910 --> 00:03:37,880
Step three.

80
00:03:37,880 --> 00:03:41,202
Four times x cubed times
two is eight x cubed.

81
00:03:41,202 --> 00:03:45,113
Six times x squared times
four is twenty four x squared.

82
00:03:45,863 --> 00:03:46,763
Step four.

83
00:03:46,712 --> 00:03:49,484
Four times x times eight is thirty two x.

84
00:03:49,484 --> 00:03:51,748
And two to the fourth is sixteen.

85
00:03:52,498 --> 00:03:57,166
So the answer is x to the fourth,
plus eight x cubed, plus twenty four

86
00:03:57,166 --> 00:04:00,258
x squared, plus thirty
two x, plus sixteen.

87
00:04:00,908 --> 00:04:02,369
Now, the exam trap.

88
00:04:02,719 --> 00:04:04,480
Expand a minus b, cubed.

89
00:04:04,480 --> 00:04:07,021
Many students write every sign as minus.

90
00:04:07,421 --> 00:04:10,468
But minus b, squared, is plus b squared.

91
00:04:10,468 --> 00:04:12,288
So the signs take turns.

92
00:04:12,288 --> 00:04:17,539
a cubed, minus three a squared b,
plus three a b squared, minus b cubed.

93
00:04:18,189 --> 00:04:19,460
Where is this asked?

94
00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:23,425
In JEE Main, as questions that expand
a sum and a difference to the same

95
00:04:23,425 --> 00:04:26,103
power and add them, so
half the terms cancel.

96
00:04:26,702 --> 00:04:27,918
Exam level now.

97
00:04:27,918 --> 00:04:32,812
Find root two plus one, to the power
four, plus root two minus one, to

98
00:04:32,812 --> 00:04:34,027
the power four.

99
00:04:34,027 --> 00:04:35,294
Pause and solve.

100
00:04:40,694 --> 00:04:42,128
The answer is B.

101
00:04:42,128 --> 00:04:43,206
Thirty four.

102
00:04:43,706 --> 00:04:46,742
Use row four: one, four, six, four, one.

103
00:04:46,742 --> 00:04:51,103
When we add, the terms with an odd
number of ones cancel, because their

104
00:04:51,103 --> 00:04:52,401
signs are opposite.

105
00:04:52,901 --> 00:04:57,718
What is left is two times: root two
to the fourth, plus six times root

106
00:04:57,718 --> 00:04:59,469
two squared, plus one.

107
00:04:59,969 --> 00:05:02,846
That is two times four
plus twelve plus one.

108
00:05:02,846 --> 00:05:05,117
Two times seventeen is thirty four.

109
00:05:05,717 --> 00:05:07,257
Here is your recap.

110
00:05:07,257 --> 00:05:08,840
Screenshot this card.

111
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:14,226
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

112
00:05:14,626 --> 00:05:15,526
One.

113
00:05:15,083 --> 00:05:18,637
What is the next row after
one, four, six, four, one?

114
00:05:19,537 --> 00:05:20,437
Two.

115
00:05:20,017 --> 00:05:23,334
How many terms are in a
plus b, to the power ten?

116
00:05:24,234 --> 00:05:25,134
Three.

117
00:05:24,925 --> 00:05:27,137
Expand a minus b, squared.

118
00:05:28,237 --> 00:05:32,979
Next time: a plus b to the power
ten, without multiplying ten times.

119
00:05:32,979 --> 00:05:34,813
Meet the binomial theorem.
